SUMMARY:Launch: PLATO
DESCRIPTION:Ariane 62 · Arianespace Plato\, for PLAnetary Transits and Os
 cillations of stars\, is a European Space Agency (ESA) mission with 26 ca
 meras to study terrestrial exoplanets in orbits up to the habitable zone 
 of Sun-like stars. Its goal is to measure the sizes of exoplanets and dis
 cover exomoons and rings around them\, as well as characterise planets' h
 ost stars by studying tiny light variations in the starlight it receives.
  (no earlier than this date) Source: Launch Library 2 (The Space Devs).
